From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 21:40:53 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] clk: samsung: zumapro: Keep the PERIC0 GPIO bus clock on

The PERIC0 GPIO gate is writable and in manual mode (CLK_CON_GAT 0x20b8
reads 0x100000: MANUAL set, automatic clock gating off). The Samsung
pin controller enables its pclk around every register access and
disables it afterwards, so each GPIO write on the block turns the gate
on and off. Stock never does this: its device tree gives zumapro's pin
controllers no clocks, so Google's pin controller never switches
the GPIO bus clocks off.

On the Pixel 9a the modem's AP2CP control lines are on this block and
toggle on every PCIe link power cycle, about twice a second during a
GNSS session. With the gate toggling, the SoC hung within 37 to 1083
link cycles in every session, at varying points, with no kernel error
and a watchdog reset. With the clock held on (a bring-up module taking
a reference) two 600 s sessions ran 1325 and 1326 link cycles each with
no hang, and the same result followed with this change in the kernel.

Mark the gate critical so the clock framework keeps it enabled.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-zumapro.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-zumapro.c b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-zumapro.c
index 2db80e4f4..a2811b7fd 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-zumapro.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/samsung/clk-zumapro.c
@@ -759,9 +759,15 @@ static const struct samsung_div_clock peric0_dividers[] __initconst = {
 	      "zumapro_mout_peric0_usi6_user", 0x1824, 0, 4, 0, CLK_DIVIDER_READ_ONLY),
 };
 
+/*
+ * The GPIO block's bus clock stays on. The gate is in manual mode (no
+ * automatic clock gating on this CMU here), and the pin controller turns
+ * it off after every register access; with the modem's AP2CP lines on
+ * this block toggling twice a second, the SoC hung within minutes.
+ */
 static const struct samsung_gate_clock peric0_gates[] __initconst = {
 	GATE(CLK_GOUT_GPIO_PERIC0, "zumapro_gpio_peric0", "zumapro_peric0_noc_user",
-	     0x20b8, 21, CLK_IGNORE_UNUSED, 0),
+	     0x20b8, 21, CLK_IS_CRITICAL, 0),
 };
 
 static const struct samsung_gate_clock peric0_ro_gates[] __initconst = {
